    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up in 1903 when the Southern Pacific Company built the Santa Susana Depot, a railroad hub that drew settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Susana%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Santa Susana Depot was later moved east along the coast route and now serves as a museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
